 ## Usage
 
 ```sh
-tally add 4.50 --category coffee
-tally list
-tally report
+tally add AMOUNT CATEGORY [--note NOTE] [--date YYYY-MM-DD]   # record an expense (negative = refund)
+tally list [-n/--limit N]                                     # most recent entries (default 10)
+tally report [--month YYYY-MM]                                # totals by category
+tally export [-o/--output FILE]                               # all entries as CSV (default: stdout)
+tally --version
 ```
 
 Entries live in `~/.tallyho.json`. Set `TALLY_FILE` to use a different file.
